From 46ae1c3665ca1e3e9ee6d843b0fbe1ac463a940b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:04:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: resolve percentage block sizes inside table cells
 like Blink

Table cells always gave their contents an indefinite block size, so
percentage heights inside a cell with a specified height behaved as auto
(amazon.com's product image, height:100% in a height:410px table cell,
rendered at its natural size over the title).

Follow Blink: replaced children resolve percentage block sizes against the
cell's fixed block size, including while rows are measured, through a new
replaced_percentage_block_size on ContainingBlockSize that anonymous blocks
pass through. After the final row sizes are known, cells with a fixed block
size, or in a table with a non-auto block size, whose layout depends on
block constraints are laid out again against their final content box, and
the row baselines are recomputed from those layouts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
